<title>CANADA: Canada Jan raw materials prices rises 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Jan raw materials prices rises 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Tuesday issued the following economic indicators for January, base</p>
<p>1986=100.</p>
<p>    INDEX			  Month pct   Yr pct    Jan index</p>
<p>    Overall raw materials     +0.1	+10.5	141.8</p>
<p>    Mineral fuels		 -0.6	+35.4	147.3</p>
<p>    Vegetable products	  +0.9	 -4.8	128.9</p>
<p>    Animals and products	-0.9	 +6.5	118.6</p>
<p>    Wood			    +1.1	 +5.4	217.0</p>
<p>    Ferrous materials	   +1.0	 -5/1	114.3</p>
<p>    Non-ferrous materials     +1.9	 -6.3	123.4</p>
<p>    Non-metallic minerals     +0.2	 +0.9	107.1</p>
<p>    Index ex mineral fuels    +0.6	 +1.5	139.3</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of economists had forecast that the overall index would rise 0.4 percent in January from December.</p>
<p>(For more information, contact Statistics Canada's Client Services Unit at (613) 951-3350 or fax: (613) 951-2848)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
